WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:09.040
Narrator: This farmer's truck is covered

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.540
in rocks, hay, and sand.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:17.230
Here's how Reece from Satisfying Clean

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:20.147
details filthy vehicles to look brand new.

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:25.513
The first step is to clear
any garbage in the interior.

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:30.318
Reece removes hay by hand

00:00:30.318 --> 00:00:32.223
because it's faster than using a vacuum.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:35.720
Next, he removes the floor
mats so he can access

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:37.778
all of the sand and dirt underneath.

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:41.990
Reece starts from the
top of the vehicle first

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:44.510
so that all of the sand
falls to the floor.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:47.276
This is the best way to
avoid double-cleaning.

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:53.390
A special wet-and-dry detailing vacuum

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:56.315
is used to remove dirt, sand, and debris.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.600
Vacuuming the floors takes the longest

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.647
but has the biggest payoff.

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:15.870
It's important to vacuum
those hard-to-reach areas

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:17.795
to try to get as much dirt and sand

00:01:17.795 --> 00:01:19.695
out of the interior as possible

00:01:19.695 --> 00:01:21.283
before moving on to the next step.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:23.841
After dry-vacuuming,

00:01:23.841 --> 00:01:26.449
Reece sprays an all-purpose
cleaner on the pedals

00:01:26.449 --> 00:01:29.467
and uses a fingernail brush
to scrub off the dirt.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.915
Next, the floor and carpets are sprayed.

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:46.020
Reece uses a drill brush
to agitate the floor.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:47.395
This releases the dirt

00:01:47.395 --> 00:01:49.511
so that it can be easily vacuumed up.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.620
It's important to always
spray the interior first

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:02.561
so that the drill brush
doesn't damage any surfaces.

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:07.770
To finish cleaning the floors,

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.800
the remainder of the dirt is vacuumed up.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:15.560
This process is repeated
throughout the vehicle

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:17.065
on different surfaces.

00:02:30.204 --> 00:02:31.262
For smaller areas,

00:02:31.262 --> 00:02:33.962
a detailing brush is used to remove dirt.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:38.970
To finish the process,
Reece sprays a polish

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:42.070
on all the interior
plastics and wipes it away

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:44.225
to reveal a bright, shiny finish.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:52.503
The process can take anywhere

00:02:52.503 --> 00:02:53.700
from two to four hours,

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.308
but farmers are always pleased

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:56.533
with the transformation.

